{{!--
  "Take this to production" card on a solution's last step. Context:
  `solution`. solution-step-actions.hbs includes it after the step actions on
  the last step only; the done panels (solution-progress.hbs and the inline
  copy in solution-step-actions.hbs) link to it by its id.

  33-solution-productionize.js drives it:
  - Plan it with Ask AI opens the drawer in productionize mode, grounded on
    the agent companion at data-sol-companion-url. Signed out it reads "Sign
    in to plan it with Ask AI". It stays hidden when the productionize
    integration is switched off, and when the companion cannot be read, the
    note below says the prompt still works.
  - Copy prompt and Preview prompt need the script (the prompt is built from
    the page's origin), so both ship hidden.
  - Connect the docs MCP server is static, and written here: the server URL,
    the Claude Code add, list and /mcp sign-in steps, the VS Code one-click
    link and version, and the anonymous allowance. They follow How to use
    these docs (docs-site), so check them when that page changes. Other
    clients are only on that page, so this card never keeps its own copy of
    their setup.
--}}
<section class="sol-panel sol-productionize" id="take-to-production" data-sol-productionize data-sol-companion-url="{{or solution.agentCompanion (concat '/solutions/' solution.id '/agent-companion.md')}}"{{#with @root.page.attributes.solution-verified-version}} data-sol-verified-version="{{this}}"{{/with}} aria-labelledby="sol-productionize-title">
  <h2 id="sol-productionize-title" class="sol-productionize-title">Take this to production</h2>
  <p class="sol-productionize-sub">Turn the reference build into a plan for your own system: your deployment, your scale, your security model.</p>
  <div class="sol-productionize-actions">
    <button type="button" class="sol-btn sol-btn--primary" data-sol-productionize-plan data-analytics="solution_productionize_start" hidden>
      <span data-sol-productionize-plan-label>Plan it with Ask AI</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="sol-btn sol-btn--ghost" data-sol-productionize-copy data-analytics="solution_productionize_copy" hidden>
      <span>Copy prompt for your coding agent</span>
    </button>
    <span class="sol-productionize-status" data-sol-productionize-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>
  <p class="sol-productionize-note" data-sol-productionize-note hidden>Ask AI can't load this solution's production guide right now. The prompt for your coding agent still works.</p>
  <details class="sol-productionize-details" data-sol-productionize-preview hidden>
    <summary>Preview prompt</summary>
    <pre class="sol-productionize-prompt" data-sol-productionize-prompt></pre>
  </details>
  <details class="sol-productionize-details" data-sol-productionize-mcp>
    <summary>Connect the docs MCP server</summary>
    <div class="sol-productionize-mcp" data-sol-mcp-block>
      <p>Connect the Redpanda docs MCP server so your agent can look up product details.<br>
      Server URL: <code>https://docs.redpanda.com/mcp</code></p>
      <p>Claude Code:</p>
      <pre class="sol-productionize-command"><code>claude mcp add --scope user --transport http redpanda https://docs.redpanda.com/mcp</code></pre>
      <p>Check it with: <code>claude mcp list</code><br>
      Sign in for a higher allowance: run <code>/mcp</code> and authenticate the <code>redpanda</code> server.</p>
      {{!-- The same install URI as Page options > Add MCP server to VS Code
            (14-markdown-dropdown.js): the server config as URI-encoded JSON. --}}
      <p>VS Code (1.102 or later, with GitHub Copilot): <a href="vscode:mcp/install?%7B%22name%22%3A%22Redpanda%20Documentation%22%2C%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.redpanda.com%2Fmcp%22%7D" data-sol-mcp-vscode>Add to VS Code</a> (one-click)</p>
      <p>Cursor, Claude Desktop, ChatGPT and other clients: see <a href="{{{relativize '/home/how-to-use-these-docs/'}}}">How to use these docs</a>.</p>
      <p>Without signing in you get 10 tool calls every 24 hours per network address.<br>
      The server answers general product questions. This solution's own production guide is the agent companion linked in the prompt.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
